typesetT -- typesetting's first slice (Tony, 2026-11-12), in firstLight: one field holds two paragraphs separated by a
blank line, wrapping in its frame, and one {styleName: text} run sits inside the second. Rows in genLadder/formsPop.sh.

firstLight's words field is the specimen. Its first paragraph is the text it always had; a blank line (written \n\n in the
form) starts the second, "A second paragraph holds {emphasis: one run} in a style of its own." emphasis is a style in
sTYLEs (IncantForms/Controls/styles): red, italic.

TY-1  the floor's own line for words: 4 lines, all 205 characters, 2 of 2 paragraphs, 1 run.
TY-2  THE BLANK LINE: between the first paragraph's last line and the second's, a band five points high across the whole
      field holds no ink.
TY-3  THE RUN: on the second paragraph's line the run's band holds red ink and no blue; before it and after it the ink is
      blue and none is red. So the style ends at the run's closing mark and the field's colour comes back.
The edge rules, on tsForm (drawn second, by what the floor says of each field):
TY-4  {{ is a literal brace: "a {{ b" is five characters, no run.
TY-5  an unknown style warns by name and the text prints plain: 5 characters, and the warning names nosuch.
TY-6  A RUN ENDS AT ITS PARAGRAPH'S END: "p {emphasis: q r" with no closing mark, a blank line, "s t": two paragraphs,
      one run, 8 characters, and no warning. (That the second paragraph is plain is the ruling; this row pins the count.)
TY-7  runs nest: 9 characters, 2 runs.
TY-8  an insertion, {name} with no colon, waits: it is left as written, 15 characters, no run.
TY-9  three paragraphs in a field too short for them: what fits is drawn, the rest is reported by name.
TY-10 a single line end inside a paragraph is a space: one paragraph, 25 characters.

T1 (2026-11-12): the text is taken apart by kant's typeset (incant/utilities) and the floor, drawSpans, reads only the span list.
Every row above reads as it did on the C++ slice but TY-5's warning, which kant now words. Rows added with T1:
  TY-11  tsCollapse  a run of spaces is one gap: "a    b" draws 3 characters.
  TY-12  tsGlue, tsAfter  a mark takes no room: x{emphasis: y}z is xyz; the space after an opening mark is dropped, and the space
         before or after a closing mark is one gap after the span before it ("y z w v", 7 characters).
  TY-13  tsWide beside tsNarrow  the gap's width comes from the style's space: with space=280 in a 300-point field each gap wraps,
         three lines where the same text in a style with no space is one.
H7 (2026-11-12, after the commit): with typeset's colour line removed TY-3 goes red; with its paragraph test off TY-1 reads one paragraph.

